<?xml version="1.0"?>
<airframe>
  <!-- How it rests when nobody says: standing on its tail (Gear.xml feet). A heading belongs to whoever places the vehicle. -->
  <rest pitch="90"/>

  <!-- No <sensors pitch="90"/>: ArduPlane flies a tailsitter in the PLANE body frame. ardupilot.org/plane/docs/guide-tailsitter.html:
       "The AHRS_ORIENTATION, the accelerometer calibration and Level trim should all be done for fixed wing flight", and in VTOL
       flight "the nose of the aircraft will try to point vertically for 'level' flight". The JSBSim body frame is that plane frame,
       so the sensors stay where they are, as standard_vtol (ArduPlane profile, no Airframe.xml) has them. The PX4 quadtailsitter
       needs the pitch-90 sensor frame; this vehicle must not copy it. The real aircraft's AHRS_ORIENTATION 2 (Yaw90, param) is a
       board-mounting rotation on that airframe, not a hover frame; a simulator param set carries 0. -->
</airframe>
